[b]WAN Affinity 0.4.2: adoption fix for always-on devices[/b]

Mixed connections already open on both WANs no longer leave a device waiting indefinitely to become sticky. In [b]both sticky and affinity modes[/b], the next new connection establishes the WAN choice and subsequent new connections follow it. Existing connections retain their WANs and NAT mappings.

Mapping lifetime now tracks the connections belonging to that mapping separately from older sessions. A private RAM checkpoint also restores verified mappings through helper restarts.

Tested on the live RT-AX88U with a separate Mac mini test: two existing HTTPS connections on different WANs, 16 concurrent new connections sharing one WAN, then a helper restart and further new connections. Both modes passed and the existing connections kept their identities, marks and NAT addresses.

[url=https://github.com/aiordanescu/asuswrt-merlin-tools/tree/main/wan-affinity]Updated downloads and installation instructions[/url]
